    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "But why does it have to be a \"shift in texture\"? Why is the goal always to endure the decay? There is a certain kind of purity in a completed work. A symphony ends. If it just kept playing forever, getting slower and more distorted, it would lose its meaning. I find myself thinking that maybe there's a grace in knowing when the curtain should fall, rather than waiting for the lights to just flicker out on their own.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
